/* Embed the application manifest as an RT_MANIFEST resource.
 *
 * Resource id 1, type 24 (RT_MANIFEST) is what Windows looks for in an EXE.
 * Embedding removes the single worst footgun in deploying this library: an
 * external `myapp.exe.manifest` has to exist *before* the first run, because
 * Windows caches the activation context by executable path and timestamp —
 * including the result when no manifest was found. Adding one afterwards
 * changes nothing until the executable is rebuilt, and the failure looks
 * exactly like a broken manifest.
 */
1 24 "app.manifest"
